--
Regression test for std::string fill construction std::string(n, c).

The fill basic_string<char>::_M_construct(size_type, _CharT) out-of-line
member used to be attached the wrong overload's body (the input-iterator
_M_construct, which refers to `__beg`) by a base-name-only match, so its
conversion failed and the constructor was a no-op.  convert_function now
repairs the member by adopting the signature-matched out-of-line definition
and its parameter names ([dcl.fct]/3), so both size() and the characters are
correct.  Grounded in N5008 [over.match] + [dcl.fct]/3.  See
doc/architectural/cpp-extern-template-member-instantiation.md.

This test was previously KNOWNBUG; it became CORE once the fix landed.
